        "ST-10": {
          "title": "Retroactive Playwright \u00a718 anti-pattern sweep (consolidated)",
          "classification": "autonomous",
          "status": "done",
          "assigned_to": "engine",
          "github_issue": 1150,
          "branch": "exec/2026-07-30__release-v8.0/EPIC-03",
          "commit_sha": "563bc4fd8f2254c2a9502d723b95d1dc89ba26f4",
          "delegation_record_id": null,
          "blocked_since_utc": null,
          "unblock_criteria": null,
          "completed_utc": "2026-07-30T20:15:00Z",
          "acceptance_verified": true,
          "spec_references": [
            "claude/system/shared_standards.md#18. Playwright Test Authoring Standard"
          ],
          "spec_reference_not_applicable": false,
          "spec_reference_not_applicable_reason": null,
          "deviations_filed": true,
          "last_completed_substep": "3.1.A.commit",
          "sign_off_record": null,
          "notes": "Grep sweep of tests/e2e/: 3 networkidle instances fixed in red-flag-journal-filter-persistence.spec.js (replaced with element-specific waits). 1 route-ordering anti-pattern fixed in trade-plan-signal-context.spec.js (generic /trade-plans/** catch-all was registered after the more specific /trade-plans/by-position/** handler and used route.continue() in its non-GET branch; reordered registration and switched to route.fallback()). 27 files use route.continue() total; the other 26 were confirmed to have no overlapping generic/specific route conflict (single-handler or non-overlapping patterns) so were not anti-patterns. Local Playwright execution unavailable in this sandbox (chromium_headless_shell not installable on this OS per playwright install output) \u2014 fixes verified via grep (zero remaining networkidle instances) and node --check syntax validation; full behavioural confirmation deferred to CI run on push."
        },
        "ST-11": {
          "title": "Test-tagging convention (smoke/regression/critical) for selective CI runs",
          "classification": "autonomous",
          "status": "done",
          "assigned_to": "engine",
          "github_issue": 1151,
          "branch": "exec/2026-07-30__release-v8.0/EPIC-03",
          "commit_sha": "5102de828ba9983ebfd5f04f1ef37c96b01acd67",
          "delegation_record_id": null,
          "blocked_since_utc": null,
          "unblock_criteria": null,
          "completed_utc": "2026-07-30T20:35:00Z",
          "acceptance_verified": true,
          "spec_references": [
            "docs/team_skills/quality/playwright_patterns.md#6. Test Tagging Convention (smoke / regression / critical) (v1.1)"
          ],
          "spec_reference_not_applicable": false,
          "spec_reference_not_applicable_reason": null,
          "deviations_filed": true,
          "last_completed_substep": "3.1.A.commit",
          "sign_off_record": null,
          "notes": "Added §6 Test Tagging Convention to docs/team_skills/quality/playwright_patterns.md (smoke/critical/regression tiers via Playwright's { tag } option; @smoke = must-pass-every-push subset, @critical = business-critical flows beyond smoke, @regression = default/remainder tier). Applied @smoke tag to the 3 tests in tests/e2e/smoke-critical-paths.spec.js (alongside existing @epic-merge-smoke). Wired selective-run into CI: .github/workflows/smoke-tests.yml now runs `npx playwright test --grep @smoke` instead of a hardcoded file path — verified via `--list` that this resolves to exactly the same 3 tests. Retroactive @critical/@regression tagging of the rest of the suite is not required per the doc's incremental-adoption note (apply at next-touch, matching the Array Guard Standard pattern)."
        },
