          "spec_reference_not_applicable": false,
          "spec_reference_not_applicable_reason": null,
          "deviations_filed": false,
          "last_completed_substep": "3.1.A.pending_commit",
          "sign_off_record": null,
          "notes": "New generator backend/test_data/generate_synthetic_trade_history.py (pure-Python generate_synthetic_trades() function, no network access, deterministic via seed) produces 25 synthetic closed trades by default — above both the SI-02 (docs/qa/si02_playwright_predesign.md, minimum_required=20) and Setup Quality Score/PT-04 (docs/specs/data_model/trade_plan_schema_audit_v4.6.md §5.2, gate not met at <20 closed trades) gate thresholds. Every record's entry_note/exit_note carries a '[SYNTHETIC TEST DATA]' tag. CLI mode (for staging/PR-preview HTTP seeding via POST /portfolio/position + POST /positions/{id}/exit, mirroring backend/test_data/seed_chart_test_data.py) refuses to run against any URL matching the same production heuristic as scripts/reset_staging_db.sh ('production' or '/prod' substring) — verified this abort path manually. 9 regression tests added and passing (tests/test_synthetic_trade_history_generator.py) covering: gate-threshold satisfaction, synthetic labelling, determinism, API-shape contract, long-only stop/entry ordering, win/loss mix, count validation, and the production-URL guard."
        }
